  "worked_solution": "The horizontal asymptote of $y={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{x}$ is $y=0.$\n\nThe vertical translation $y={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{x}+c$ shifts the asymptote to $y=c.$\n\nIn the graph above, the horizontal asymptote is $y=1.$ Therefore, $c=1.$",
